\bibcite{arriola2024blockdiffusion}{{1}{2024}{{Arriola et~al.}}{{}}}
\newlabel{fig:dflash-fail}{{4}{6}{DFlash branch-cache failure (held constant: Qwen3-8B verifier, output length~$32$, greedy, fixed branch template). Bars: throughput under four prediction settings (\textsc {Exact}, \textsc {Pred+Off+Oracle}, \textsc {Pred+On+Oracle}, \textsc {Pred+On+Normal}). Lines: the corresponding cache-hit rate. Under the realized predictor (\textsc {Pred+On+Normal}, red), the cache-hit rate stays near $0.1$ across all batch sizes, and throughput drops to a fraction of \textsc {Exact}. Under an \emph {oracle} predictor (\textsc {Pred+On+Oracle}, green) the hit rate jumps to ${\sim }0.95$ but throughput still does not exceed \textsc {Exact}---confirming that the \emph {architecture}, not just the predictor, is the binding constraint for DFlash}{figure.caption.6}{}}
